Study on Construction Risks and Countermeasures of Heping Avenue Southward Line in Wuhan
REN Shifang1,2, TU Wenbo3 (1. CCCC Second Harbor Engineering Co., Ltd,., Wuhan., Hubei 430040, China; 2. China Railway Major Bridge Reconnaissance & Design Institute Co., Ltd., Wuhan, Hubei 430040, China; 3. School of Transportation Engineering, East China Jiaotong University, Nanchang, Jiangxi 330299, China)
Abstract: In the South Extension Project of Heping Avenue in Wuhan, there are problems such as long construction distance and
large section of the shield, the shield tunneling process traverses the Huanghelou Scenic Area, old shantytowns in Wuchang, and
the Beijing-Guangzhou Railway, parallel approach to subway line 5. The geological conditions along the route are intricate,
encompassing highly developed karst regions, areas with unevenly distributed soft and hard soil strata, and hard rocks, which are
prone to causing tool wear, cave collapse, water inrushes, requiring frequent tool changes and pressure opening operation,
significantly impeding the progress of shield tunneling and posing considerable safety hazards. In light of these challenges,
targeted optimizations have been implemented in the design and selection of shield tunneling machines, equipped with specialized
wear detection devices, rolling cutter load monitoring systems, SSP-E advanced detectors, sophisticated geological drilling
systems, and tunnel grouting systems. Construction parameters and corresponding measures have been devised for traversing
different geological sections and sensitive environmental areas, effectively ensuring the smooth and safe execution of the shield
tunneling construction.
Keywords tunnels; shield; sensitive buildings; risk; construction
